\details{
Reads \code{.pkx} projects, which share the \code{.mlxtran} section syntax. The input
files are the data file and the model used by compartmental analysis
(\verb{<MODEL>} \verb{[LONGITUDINAL]}), when the project has one. The output
directory is the \code{exportpath} of \verb{<PKANALIX>} \verb{[SETTINGS]}, or the project
name next to the project file without one.

Results are read from \verb{PKanalix/IndividualParameters/} in the output
directory, one folder per task: \code{nca/ncaIndividualParameters.txt},
\code{ca/caIndividualParameters.txt}, \code{ca/cost.txt} and
\verb{be/confidenceInterval_<formulation>.txt}. They give the tasks with results
(\code{tasks}, in the order \verb{nca,ca,be}), the number of individuals
(\code{n_individuals}, unique \code{id} in the NCA parameters, else in the CA
parameters), the CA criteria (\verb{-2LL} as \code{ofv}, \code{AIC} as \code{aic}, \code{BIC} as
\code{bic}, \code{Cost} as \code{ca_cost}) and, per formulation and parameter, the
bioequivalence ratio, its confidence interval and conclusion.
}
